RUN 2, 2026-09-12 from 11:38 AEST, on the restored simulator: the happy path, all the way through bob's sweep. Run 1
(2026-09-11, interrupted after alice's Claim by a stall of the companion's own, since fixed) is kept at the end of this
file. Machine paths are written <tmp>, <repo> and <user>.

Each party is its own OS process running the xmrswap binary, with its own state file, its own DERO wallet (simulator
30006 bob, 30007 alice), its own monero-wallet-rpc (regtest :28084 bob, :28083 alice) and one shared -channel
directory. Wallets 30010-30013 (the swap board, and the Zcash engineer's test running at the same time) were not used.

How it was run, and what differs from a mainnet run
- The binary: built with go1.26.8 from the committed tree, sha256 5c3a39c014074440f0b59251b1b6b3af6445d0948fa575deb1b1ce1404212216.
  It carries everything through MT-B26, and the owner-only ACL set through the Windows API (no icacls): the fix for
  run 1's stall.
- -net regtest against the DERO simulator (the only DERO network -net regtest is accepted with). Not testnet or mainnet.
  The simulator had been wiped and restored the same morning; wallets 30006 and 30007 had no transfer after height 173.
- -htlc was NOT given: each companion took the scid deploy/networks.json records for the simulator,
  9422717ff20a5ff90d791e10a1c4b0618f232de2c36770a8f74303857fa043ab (MT-A18), and checked its code against the pinned
  htlc.bas v2 before reading anything from it.
- -monerod 127.0.0.1:28081 on both: each companion names that monerod to its wallet-rpc after every open and generate.
- Logins from the environment only: VEIL_RPC_LOGIN and XMRSWAP_MONERO_LOGIN were set, and no login is on either command
  line. The simulator wallets and the regtest wallet-rpc run without logins, so both companions warn (as they must off
  mainnet) that the wallets answered without credentials; on mainnet they would refuse to start.
- The channel is sealed (GAP-019): the maker's key came from `xmrswap channel-key`, and both processes read it from
  XMRSWAP_CHANNEL_KEY. Its value is written nowhere.
- The prover: the reproducible proof-xmr build (sha256 7293e9c9..., the current ProverSHA256, MT-B26), in WSL. The
  command line runs on Windows, because WSL here is in NAT mode and cannot reach the simulator, which listens on
  127.0.0.1 only; and -prover must be the absolute path of a binary the companion executes directly, which the Linux
  build is not, from Windows. So -prover names a scratch wrapper (proverwrap.exe, not in the repository) that hashes
  the WSL binary against 7293e9c9... before every run and then runs it through wsl.exe; the command line pins the
  wrapper with -prover-sha256, which it accepts off mainnet only and warns about.
- MT-B09: alice was given two -daemon, 127.0.0.1:20000 and localhost:20000 — the same simulator node under two names.
  That exercises the witness path; it is not an independent node, and the simulator has no second one.
- Monero blocks: nothing mines on a regtest chain by itself, so the driver script mined one block about every 6 s.
- Policy: the command line's own defaults (t1 = t1-min + 20 = 420 blocks, t2 = t1 + 400, G = 100, 20 confirmations,
  stable 8, claim margin 8), the stipend at its default. Nothing was lowered.

