The wake, at the end
  Alice's companion removed its own wake task when her swap ended, and the Task Scheduler holds no xmrswap task
  after the run. Bob's companion, which registered no wake, tried to remove one under its own swap id and said "the
  wake task xmrswap-8be3f2a7116e984c was not removed (Unregister-ScheduledTask: exit status 1)": that PowerShell cmdlet
  fails on a name it does not find, whatever -ErrorAction says. A false alarm with nothing behind it, since fixed: the
  companion now removes a task only when it is there (TestRemovingAWakeThatIsNotThereIsNoError).

Left behind on purpose
  The joint wallets xmrswap-9422717f-8be3f2a7116e984c-0-spend and -view stay in bob's wallet-rpc wallet-dir inside WSL,
  encrypted under the swap's password: -monero-wallet-dir (required on mainnet) was not given, so the companion said
  so rather than deleting files it cannot reach.

