  Not reached: bob's sweep, and each side's record of its end. On disk bob stayed in "claimed" and alice in "claiming":
  both had done their part on the chain (the Claim was mined and stable), and neither could write that down.

The stall, and its cause
  From 20:24:59 every state save of both processes failed: the owner-only ACL step (GAP-020) runs icacls.exe on every
  write, and each icacls died at start with exit status 0xc0000142 (STATUS_DLL_INIT_FAILED): 2464 failed saves for
  alice, 879 for bob. Every save before 20:24:59 had succeeded. The time matches the pause killing this session's
  background shells, whose console the companions had inherited: a running process survives that, but a new console
  program it starts cannot initialise. The companion fails closed without durable state, so neither side moved on —
  no coins at risk (regtest and simulator coins; the Claim was already on the chain; bob's state holds s_a + s_b), but
  a swap stopped by the machine, not by the protocol. The defect is the companion's: it depends on starting a console
  program for every write, and anything that stops that — a closed terminal, a service context, a lost session,
  antivirus — stops the swap. Fixed: the ACL is now set through the Windows API, with no program started (tools/xmrswap/acl_windows.go; TestOwnerOnlyACLStartsNoProgram runs with nothing reachable on PATH, and fails on the icacls version: exec: "icacls": executable file not found).

What differs from the committed state of the prover pin
  This run's wrapper checked the pin of the day, 4d3bde0a... (the checkout-bound release build). The pin has since
  moved to the reproducible build 7293e9c9... (MT-B26); the rerun uses that.

